Apple hired former American Airlines executive vice president Nick Gatten as its new vice president of government affairs, reports <em><a href="https://www.bloomberg.com/news/articles/2026-08-12/apple-taps-american-airlines-veteran-as-government-affairs-head">Bloomberg</a></em>.<br/>
<br/>
<img src="https://images.macrumors.com/article-new/2023/11/Apple-Logo-16x9.jpg" alt="" width="1200" height="630" class="aligncenter size-full wp-image-924188" /><br/>
Gatten will take on some of the duties of senior vice president of government affairs Katherine Adams, who is retiring at the end of 2026. Gatten will report to Apple senior vice president and general counsel Jennifer Newstead, with Adams to remain available in an advisory role until October 1.<br/>
<br/>
<em>Bloomberg</em> says Gatten is a Republican that Apple felt would be able to align with the Trump administration. He previously worked at Fannie Mae where he managed a team that interfaced with Republican members of Congress, and he also oversaw government affairs at JPMorgan Chase &amp; Co. and American Airlines.<br/>
<br/>
Gatten will work closely with <a href="https://www.macrumors.com/guide/tim-cook/">Tim Cook</a> in his new role. Cook plans to step down as Apple CEO on September 1, with hardware chief John Ternus to take over. Cook will remain on as executive chairman, engaging with policymakers and governments worldwide.<br/>This article, &quot;<a href="https://www.macrumors.com/2026/08/12/apple-vice-president-government-affairs/">Apple Hires Airline Exec as Vice President of Government Affairs</a>&quot; first appeared on <a href="https://www.macrumors.com">MacRumors.com</a><br/><br/><a href="https://forums.macrumors.com/threads/apple-hires-airline-exec-as-vice-president-of-government-affairs.2486826/">Discuss this article</a> in our forums<br/><br/>